- description: Queries ABOM runs against ABOM's own workflows

# Narrower than abom-findings.qls on purpose. This suite is a gate on one repository at review
# time, not the attribution corpus: a finding here has to be worth blocking a pull request
# for, so the experimental queries that abom-findings.qls keeps are absent.
- import: codeql-suites/actions-security-and-quality.qls
  from: codeql/actions-queries
  version: 0.6.35

# Retains `Debug/SyntaxError` and `Diagnostics/SuccessfullyExtractedFiles`, which the upstream
# suite includes and which report nothing about security. They stay because a self audit that
# cannot distinguish "no findings" from "nothing was extracted" is worse than no self audit.

# `unpinned-tag` reports a `uses:` naming a tag rather than a commit, trusting only the `actions`
# and `github` orgs. It reads the ref and never `.github/workflows/actions.lock`, which resolves
# every `uses:` here to a commit and is what a diff shows when one moves. `gh actions-lock`
# rewrites an inline SHA back to a narrowed semver tag, so in this repository a tag *is* the
# pinned form and the rule fires on every third-party action the repository will ever add --
# measured 2026-09-20, on `golangci/golangci-lint-action@v9.3.0` and
# `peter-evans/create-pull-request@v8.1.1`, both of which the lockfile resolves to a commit.
#
# TEMPORARY. `codeql/actions-queries` 0.6.36 makes the rule read the lockfile, at which point this
# exclusion is wrong rather than merely unnecessary. 0.6.35 is the latest published as of
# 2026-09-20; delete this on the upgrade that resolves 0.6.36 or later.
#
# Excluded here and not in `abom-findings.qls`: a repository ABOM analyzes has no lockfile of ours
# to vouch for it, so the finding is still collected and attributed.
- exclude:
    id: actions/unpinned-tag

# What replaces it, so the gate is not left with nothing that reads the lockfile. It asks the
# question the excluded rule cannot: not whether a ref *looks* pinned, but whether the lockfile
# accounts for it. Stricter than upstream ever was here -- no trusted-owner exemption, and a bare
# commit is not taken on faith.
- query: ActionsLockAware/UncoveredActionRef.ql
  from: advanced-security/abom-actions-findings-src
